---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {englishThemes} from '../../../data/themes-en';
import {estrofasDeCanto} from '../../../lib/corpus';
export function getStaticPaths(){return englishThemes.map(theme=>({params:{slug:theme.slug},props:{theme}}))}
const {theme}=Astro.props;
const stanza=estrofasDeCanto(theme.part,theme.canto)[0];
const related=englishThemes.filter(x=>x.slug!==theme.slug);
---
<Base lang="en-US" pageType="Article" title={`${theme.title} — Martín Fierro English Themes`} description={theme.lead}>
<article class="theme"><nav><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / <a href="/en/themes/">Six themes</a> / {theme.title}</nav><p class="eyebrow">CRITICAL READING · MARTÍN FIERRO</p><h1>{theme.title}</h1><p class="lead">{theme.lead}</p><section><h2>Reading the poem</h2><p>{theme.analysis}</p><p>Rather than treating Fierro as a neutral chronicler, distinguish the fictional speaker, the historical setting and modern interpretation. This reading is an editorial guide, not an original section of the poem.</p></section><section><h2>A primary-text passage</h2>{stanza&&<figure><blockquote lang="es">{stanza.versos.slice(0,6).map(v=><span>{v.texto}</span>)}</blockquote><figcaption>José Hernández · {theme.part==='ida'?'Part One (1872)':'Part Two (1879)'} · Canto {theme.canto} · stanza {stanza.numero}. {stanza.versos.length>6?'First six lines only.':'Complete stanza.'} Original Spanish preserved from the shared corpus.</figcaption></figure>}<p><a href={`/leer/${theme.part}/${theme.canto}/#${stanza?.id??''}`} lang="es">Verify this passage in the original poem (Spanish)</a> · <a href={`/en/students/${theme.part==='ida'?'canto':'vuelta-canto'}-${theme.canto}/`}>English canto guide</a></p></section><section><h2>Discussion question</h2><p>{theme.question}</p><h2>Sources and reading context</h2><p>Primary text: the poem's single structured corpus, reproduced without changes. Historical and institutional starting point: <a href={theme.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">consult the documented external reference</a>. Literary analysis is editorial and should not be mistaken for a verified account of every historical community.</p></section><footer><h2>Explore another theme</h2><div class="related">{related.map(x=><a href={`/en/themes/${x.slug}/`}>{x.title}</a>)}</div></footer></article>
<style>.theme{max-width:970px;margin:30px auto 90px;color:#30271d}.theme a{color:#85402c}.theme h1{font:600 clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4.3rem)/1.1 Georgia,serif}.theme h2{font:600 2rem Georgia,serif}.theme p{font:1.08rem/1.75 Georgia,serif}.lead{font-size:1.25rem!important}.eyebrow{font:700 .73rem system-ui,sans-serif!important;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#92503a}.theme section{margin:40px 0}.theme figure{background:#eee3d4;padding:23px}.theme blockquote{font:1.14rem/1.7 Georgia,serif;margin:0}.theme blockquote span{display:block}.theme figcaption{font:.8rem/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;margin-top:13px}.related{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 20px}.related a{font:.9rem system-ui,sans-serif}@media(max-width:680px){.theme{padding:0 12px}}</style>
</Base>